<Analysis>
<![CDATA[ (9/16) Not only do the Angels rank dead-last in MLB with 24 saves, they're 1 of only 3 teams with fewer than 30. Los Angeles was very active at the trade deadline, dealing away relievers Ryan Zeferjahn, Kirby Yates and Brent Suter after previously DFA'ing Jordan Romano. That means nearly half of the team's saves have come from players no longer pitching for the Angels. Since then, Ben Joyce, Ryan Watson and Samy Natera have taken on the bulk of high-leverage work in the late innings. Joyce didn't make his 2026 season debut until August, but the flamethrowing right-hander now leads Los Angeles with 5 saves. He's likely to finish out 2026 as the Angels' closer, but the team probably won't have a reliever with double-digit saves this season. ]]>
