<![CDATA[ (9/15) After a disappointing 2025, Atlanta is back on top of the NL East division (+4.5 games) with two weeks remaining in the 2026 campaign. The strength of Atlanta's bullpen is big reason why, as their 3.42 collective ERA ranks 3rd. While 10 different Braves have recorded saves this season, 12-year veteran, Raisel Iglesias, has accounted for the majority of them, racking up 32 (8th) through mid-September. His 69% team save share isn't as high as his past two campaigns, but Iglesias continues to get the job done in the ninth inning when called upon. Robert Suarez (elbow) has been out since late-June, but could be back before the end of the season and playoffs. Didier Fuentes has emerged as a reliable multi-inning setup man while also picking up a few saves along the way. ]]>
