<Analysis>
<![CDATA[ (9/16) 10 different White Sox pitchers have combined for the team's 38 saves through mid-September. Seranthony Dominguez - who was Chicago's Opening Day closer but was subsequently traded to Seattle - still leads the team with 12 saves and is the only reliever in double-digits. Grant Taylor and Bryan Hudson - who currently top this hierarchy - are tied for 2nd on the team with 8 saves apiece. Thus far, the White Sox only have 1 save in the month of September, which went to Hudson. Hudson has actually recorded the White Sox' past 3 saves dating back to late-August. Taylor has struggled in recent appearances - he's permitted at least 1 ER in 4 straight outings - but has been dominant at times through 2026 and remains in the picture for the team's highest-leverage moments in the late-innings. Keep an eye on LHP Hagen Smith, whose performance through his first 22 major-league innings has been outstanding. He has yet to pitch regularly in the late innings, but he could (and probably should) be pitching some important innings for the White Sox down the stretch. ]]>
</Analysis>
